# TypeScript Standards

- **API** (`apps/api`): semicolons, single quotes (Prettier), `strictNullChecks` + decorators
- **Web** (`apps/web`): no semicolons in app code (Vite style), `verbatimModuleSyntax`, strict unused locals
- Use explicit return types on Nest controllers/services when adding public methods
- Prefer `import type` when importing types only (web `verbatimModuleSyntax`)

```typescript
// ✅ API — Nest injectable + controller
@Injectable()
export class AppService {
  getHello(): string {
    return 'Hello World!';
  }
}

// ✅ Web — functional component + named hooks import
import { useState } from 'react'
function App() { /* ... */ }
export default App

// ❌ Avoid mixing web style (no semicolons) into API files or vice versa
```
